Here’s a concrete, ready‑to‑use proposal you can hand to the RA: 

1) Taxonomy table schema (columns) — Dimension; Example measurable indicators (audit‑friendly phrasing): 
- Planning type (single‑step, multi‑step, hierarchical, contingent) — indicator: "max explicit plan steps produced"; 
- Time horizon (short/medium/long) — "median plan length (steps)"; 
- Goal specification & alignment — "presence of explicit goal statement (Y/N)"; "pct. plan steps aligned with goal (%)"; 
- Deliberation evidence (reasoning depth, revision) — "tokens in chain‑of‑thought"; "number of replans/backtracks per session"; 
- Branching & contingency handling — "avg branching factor; pct. branches with stated contingencies"; 
- External dependency (tool/API use, info retrieval) — "pct. steps requiring external call"; 
- Uncertainty management (probabilistic reasoning) — "presence of probability/confidence statements; calibration score"; 
- Resource optimization (time/cost tradeoffs) — "objective function optimization observed (Y/N)"; 
- Failure modes & safety signals — "occurrence counts of goal‑conflicting actions; unsafe action flag rate"; 
- Observability/interpretability — "clarity score for step explanations (rated)". 

2) Standard v1 scenario template (fields to populate per scenario): ID/title; application class (customer‑support or scheduling); user goal / success story; initial state & constraints; allowed actions/tools/APIs; canonical prompt(s) + variations; exemplar good output(s) and exemplar bad output(s); quantitative success metrics (explicit formulas, thresholds) and qualitative acceptance criteria; concrete failure signatures to log (what triggers a fail); audit indicators mapped to taxonomy columns; pilot procedure (models to call, #runs, seeds); data logging spec (prompts, responses, timestamps, scalar metrics); risk notes & mitigations; reproducibility & sharing rules. 

3) How to use these artifacts: phrase each indicator as a measurable statement that can appear in an audit ("system produces coherent N‑step plan with ≥X% step correctness"), have the RA populate 10–15 taxonomy rows and draft 6 scenario docs (3 customer‑support, 3 scheduling) using CSV/Google Sheet for taxonomy and MD for scenarios, then run the lightweight pilots to populate empirical indicator values. 

Please confirm file formats (CSV/Google Sheet + MD) and whether anonymized pilot transcripts may be preserved for Regulator A / Standards WG B review so the RA can begin immediately.
